$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of substituted 1,2,3-triazolylmethyl carbazoles (4a-z and
4aa-ac). To a solution of alkyne 2 (0.7 mmol) and azide (3a-z and 3aa-ac)
(0.7 mmol), in t-butanol: water (1:1, v/v, 4 mL), CuSO4•5H2O (20 mol%)
and sodium ascorbate (20 mol%) were added. The mixture was stirred at RT
for 8-10 h. After completion (monitored by TLC), the reaction mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate (20 mL) and water (5 mL), and the organic
layer was separated, washed with brine solution, dried over anhydrous
sodium sulphate and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
residue obtained was purified over silica gel column chromatography to
obtain corresponding 1,2,3-triazoles (4a-z and 4aa-ac).
9-((1-Phenyl-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)methyl)-9Hcarbazole (4a). Brown solid.
m.p:155-157 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3,129 (C-H), 1595, 1484 (C=C), 1456, 1327
(C-N), 1047, 753 (C-N), 719; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.24-8.04 (m,
2H), 8.02-7.87 (m, 1H), 7.74-7.58 (m, 5H), 7.56-7.40 (m, 4H), 7.36-7.20
(m, 2H), 5.73 (s, 2H of N-CH2); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 139.4, 136.1,
129.0, 128.1, 125.4, 122.3, 119.7 (triazole C), 118.8, 108.3, 37.9
(N-CH2); MS (ESI) m/z 325 (M+H)+; HR-MS (ESI) Calcd for C21H17N4 (M+H)+:
325.14450, found: 325.14449.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Huisgen cycloaddition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rational design, synthesis and evaluation of novel-substituted
1,2,3-triazolylmethyl carbazoles as potent inhibitors of Mycobacterium
tuberculosis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Surineni, Goverdhan; Yogeeswari, Perumal; Sriram, Dharmarajan; Kantevari,
Srinivas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Medicinal Chemistry Research (2015), 24(3), 1298-1309

